Wait, that's not quite right. With the shared memory approach, each block computes inv_freq (32 expf calls). For Q: 4 blocks × 32 expf = 128. For K: 1 block × 32 expf = 32. Total per layer: 160 expf. Per token: 160 × 22 = 3,520 expf. At ~20 cycles each: ~70,400 cycles. Plus 25,344 shared memory reads.

Without optimization: 25,344 pow(double) calls. Each pow takes ~200 cycles (double precision). Total: ~5M cycles.

So the speedup for the inv_freq computation alone would be ~70x. But this is just the inv_freq part; the sincos and memory operations also take time. Still, this should be a significant improvement.

